@startuml
title AWS Cost Dashboard – S3 Webhook Automatic Import Flow

actor "External User" as ExtUser
participant "AWS S3\nBucket" as S3
participant "AWS SNS\nTopic" as SNS
participant "ngrok\nTunnel" as ngrok
participant "API Route" as API
participant "S3WebhookController" as WebhookController
participant "AwsS3Service" as S3Service
participant "CsvParser" as Parser
participant "CsvReportToData" as DataOps
database PostgreSQL as DB

ExtUser -> S3 : Upload CSV to\ns3://fyp-acd/cost-reports/2025/12/
S3 -> S3 : Trigger ObjectCreated event
S3 -> SNS : Publish event notification

SNS -> ngrok : POST webhook\n(HTTPS notification)
ngrok -> API : Forward to\nPOST /api/aws/s3/webhook

API -> WebhookController : handleS3Event(Request)
WebhookController -> WebhookController : Parse SNS message\nExtract S3 object key

WebhookController -> S3Service : downloadFile(s3Key)
S3Service -> S3 : GET object
S3 --> S3Service : file content
S3Service --> WebhookController : CSV content

WebhookController -> Parser : parse(content)
Parser --> WebhookController : parsed data

WebhookController -> Parser : processRows(data)
Parser --> WebhookController : raw cost data

WebhookController -> DataOps : processData(rawData)
DataOps --> WebhookController : processed data

WebhookController -> DataOps : saveToDatabase(systemUserId, data)
DataOps -> DB : INSERT INTO cost_uploads
DataOps -> DB : BATCH INSERT INTO cost_records
DB --> DataOps : success
DataOps --> WebhookController : upload record

WebhookController --> API : 200 OK response
API --> SNS : HTTP 200 OK

note right of DB
  File automatically imported
  without user intervention!
end note
@enduml